DC2-PROGRAM.md-43-  Poisson-commuting polynomials on a 4-dim symplectic space have **trdeg ≤ 2** (max
DC2-PROGRAM.md-44-  Poisson-commutative subalgebras have trdeg n = 2) — so leading data is 2-dimensional,
DC2-PROGRAM.md:45:  the quantum analogue of Dixmier's "leading forms are powers of a common form" in A_1;
