DC2-PROGRAM.md-157-- **Strips**: in A_1, Poisson-commuting leading forms in 2 commutative variables are
DC2-PROGRAM.md:158:  proportional powers ⇒ polygons are strips along a common direction (Dixmier's lemma =
DC2-PROGRAM.md-159-  the abelian top-edges-through-origin picture). In A_2, trdeg of a Poisson-commutative
DC2-PROGRAM.md-160-  subalgebra ≤ 2 ⇒ the four leading forms at any admissible w are algebraically
DC2-PROGRAM.md-161-  dependent through a 2-dim family: polytope faces of all four generators share a common
DC2-PROGRAM.md-162-  2-dimensional "shadow". The A_2 strip analogue = polytopes thin transverse to a common
DC2-PROGRAM.md-163-  2-face. Making this precise (which 2-faces can occur, after normalizing by tame
DC2-PROGRAM.md-164-  automorphisms) is the A_2 replacement for GGV's subrectangular classification — open,
DC2-PROGRAM.md-165-  and the natural first theorem of the program.
