DC2-PROGRAM.md-314-Replacing one-variable Schur/centralizer rigidity with *any finiteness mechanism* for
DC2-PROGRAM.md-315-CCR quadruples. In A_1, [Q,P] = 1 lives inside a commutative, rank-bounded centralizer
DC2-PROGRAM.md:316:after one normalization — that finiteness is what every known DC(1) argument (Dixmier's
DC2-PROGRAM.md-317-low-degree cases, Joseph, Zheglov) ultimately spends. In A_2 nothing bounds the
DC2-PROGRAM.md-318-quadruple: centralizers of single elements contain Weyl subalgebras, polytopes live in
DC2-PROGRAM.md-319-ℤ⁴ with a 2-parameter leading-form family, and the tame normalization group is small
DC2-PROGRAM.md-320-relative to the shape space. No candidate mechanism exists in the literature. Second
DC2-PROGRAM.md-321-hardest: proving quantization rigidity (every PC_2 counterexample fails to lift to A_2)
DC2-PROGRAM.md-322-— currently not even conjecturally structured, but ¬PC_2 makes it exactly the content
