APPROACHES.md-18-2. All three agree the tried core — GGV corner farm, Sigray sheet books, formal-germ D-series — is a necessary-condition mill stuck on the same two gaps: **no landing theorem and no topological-degree ceiling** (Fable's G1/G2/G5 = Grok's REDUCTION.md audit = Sol's "two global bridges").
APPROACHES.md-19-3. The strip/residue-ODE result (S5–S6/G3) is the campaign's one real theorem; scope-limited, and the ODE rigidity has Żołądek A.7 priority.
APPROACHES.md-20-4. The implication ladder above JC2 (Mathieu, GMC n≥3, PC(2), JC(n≥3), Hessian n≠4) is dead post-July-2026 — full consensus; Fable's "no n=2 traction anywhere" matches Grok's "documented massacre".
APPROACHES.md-21-5. Char-p: Mondello verified, W2 Witt obstruction total on the searched stratum (1,152/1,152); the odd-prime/other-support refinement is the agreed open extension (F16 = S31's 5/10 = G17(i)–(iii)).
APPROACHES.md-22-6. Promise scores are incommensurable across surveys (see semantics note above); this document flags disagreements rather than averaging them.
