xmodel/sol-dixmier.log-370-ZHEGLOV-SCOPE.md:15:**Theorem chain:** ¬DC1 ⇒ subrectangular DC-pair [GGV, S3] ⇒ T:DC-pairs + T:subrectangular_sequence [S4] ⇒ family Φ_{N,1}-pairs with controlled sequences [L:Phi_N(P)] ⇒ string↔commutative correspondence [S5] transports to rank-1 spectral side ⇒ distinguished-coefficient computation contradicts N-independence [S6 Steps 4–7]. Normal forms (S2) are the ambient machinery for every step after S3.
xmodel/sol-dixmier.log-371-ZHEGLOV-SCOPE.md:17:**External load-bearing inputs (not reproved here):** [GZ1] (arXiv 2303.10306, Guo–Zheglov normal forms — the whole calculus), [A.Z] (generalized Schur theory), [GGV] (subrectangular reduction of minimal counterexamples), Wilson's theorem, classical Schur–Sato. An error in [GZ1] would sink the paper wholesale.
xmodel/sol-dixmier.log-372-ZHEGLOV-SCOPE.md:27:**R1. Endgame conjugation calculation, S6 Steps 4–7 (lines 3220–3390).** Hand symbolic computation in the bespoke vector-form calculus (Γ_1, Γ_2, σ-shifts, ∫-symbols): computes S̄_{−N−1}, γ_1=−a/(ln+Ndn)+dn/2, γ_2=−d_2/(2(Nd_2+l_2)), then E:tildeQ_N,I giving A=½d(M̃_{I−1}+1)(dn−M̃_{I−1}−1), B, C; then L:tail averaging; final c_{N,I;r(I)} formula. One sign/offset error anywhere destroys the contradiction. This is exactly the part "simplified" in v5 — i.e., rewritten twice (v4, v5). Includes the one-line inequality claim **A≠0** (line 3256, argument compressed: M̃_{I−1}=ord(Q_{I−1})nd−M_{I−1} forces dn−M̃_{I−1}−1≠0).
