xmodel/sol-dixmier.log-375-ZHEGLOV-SCOPE.md:53:- **T1. CHEAPEST FALSIFICATION EXPERIMENT: random-test L:polynomials** (line 1721). Unconditional polynomial claim: for g̃ with ≥2 distinct roots, c̃g̃^A = H'g̃−((z̃+1)/d̃)Hg̃' has a polynomial solution H only if l̃/d̃∈N, l̃/d̃>1, and then deg H=l̃(z̃+1)/d̃. Test = linear solve in coeffs of H over QQ for random (g̃,A,d̃,z̃=(A−1)d̃), including adversarial families (clustered roots, l̃/d̃ boundary cases). **~2-3 agent-h.** A single counterexample kills the S4 engine (used at lines 2041, 2198, 2301 to force the case exhaustions) ⇒ proof collapses.
