xmodel/sol-dixmier.log-1283-Source: `zheglov/v5src/DC5.tex` (3539 lines). Sections + line ranges:
xmodel/sol-dixmier.log-1284-- **S1 Intro** (171–565): full proof scheme + notation list.
xmodel/sol-dixmier.log:1285:- **S2 Preliminaries, theory of normal forms** (565–1300, ~735 ln): imports from [A.Z]=Zheglov's generalized Schur theory, [GZ1]=Guo–Zheglov normal forms, Dixmier, Wilson, Sato. Ring tower A_1 ⊂ D_1=K[[x]][∂] ⊂ D̂_1^sym; Schur operator S with SPS⁻¹=∂^p; centralizer C(∂^p) ≅ M_p(K[D^p]), "vector form". Mostly cited, not reproved.
xmodel/sol-dixmier.log-1286-- **S3 DC-pairs** (1300–1451): counterexample = DC-pair; reduction to *subrectangular* Newton-polygon type (from [GGV] minimal-counterexample results); L:9 from [GZ] (Berest-conjecture paper).
xmodel/sol-dixmier.log-1287-- **S4 Main preparatory theorems** (1451–2357, ~906 ln, biggest): **T:DC-pairs** (head-chopping process terminates, distance maximal = p+q−1) and **T:subrectangular_sequence** (all F_i(P,Q) subrectangular; edge polynomials f_{0,1}, f_{1,0} identified). Inductive engine: L:Q_p (tail shape), **L:induction_step** (1575), **L:polynomials** (1721, "key lemma", uses subrectangularity), **L:induction_step1** (1853).
xmodel/sol-dixmier.log-1288-- **S5 String equation** (2357–2825, added in v4): [Q,P]=1 for general ODOs; bijection {string solutions with terminating head-chopping} ↔ {rank-1 commuting pairs} via cutting/glueing the tail (T:string_equation 2547, T:one-to-one-correspondence 2620/2727, T:inverse_string_equation 2748). Extends A. Schwarz's coprime-order correspondence to **non-coprime orders** — needed because subrectangular DC-pairs have non-coprime orders.
xmodel/sol-dixmier.log-1289-- **S6 Proof of T:main** (2825–3539): 6a Preliminary lemmas (2842–3120): build modified pair P_n,Q_n then family Φ_{N,1}(P_n),Φ_{N,1}(Q_n) parametrized by N; **L:Phi_N(P)** (two cases, sequence lengths, distance head↔tail = N+1). 6b **"Some explicit calculations"** (3120–3539, ~420 ln): pass to Puiseux series X_{N,n} solving f(D̃^p,X)=0 (BC-type polynomial); **contradiction**: distinguished coefficient at D̃^{−ord P'} is N-independent (L:distinguished coefficients, via series-similarity X_{N1}=X_{N2}|_{D̃↦D̃^r}) yet Steps 4–7 compute it to be N-dependent. QED by contradiction.
xmodel/sol-dixmier.log-1290-
xmodel/sol-dixmier.log-1291-**Theorem chain:** ¬DC1 ⇒ subrectangular DC-pair [GGV, S3] ⇒ T:DC-pairs + T:subrectangular_sequence [S4] ⇒ family Φ_{N,1}-pairs with controlled sequences [L:Phi_N(P)] ⇒ string↔commutative correspondence [S5] transports to rank-1 spectral side ⇒ distinguished-coefficient computation contradicts N-independence [S6 Steps 4–7]. Normal forms (S2) are the ambient machinery for every step after S3.
