./RECON.md-71-- **Gao 2608.00222** (v1 2026-07-31): "tangent-sweep mechanism" — sweeping tangent lines of plane curves ("classical duality forces the map to hit most points several times"), generalized to direction fields on hypersurfaces. Explicit maps: 3D deg 4; 4D deg 5, 10; 5D deg 6, 12; arbitrarily large geometric degree per dimension. **Does not address dim 2 at all.** Credits Alpöge (07-19), Gallagher (07-20), Speyer (07-23). [USABLE-BY-US as negative-space: a second mechanism, still silent on the plane]
./RECON.md-72-- **Shaska 2607.20210v2** (v1 07-22 14 KB → v2 07-25 44 KB, tripled): notes the Alpöge map is equivariant for wt(x,y,z)=(1,−1,−2); proves (i) all-positive-weight equivariant Keller maps are automorphisms (no counterexample can be graded that way), and (ii) **in dimension two the automorphism conclusion holds for EVERY weight sign pattern** — i.e., no graded/equivariant plane counterexample exists. Also Kummer-condition observations on stacky strata. No Newton-polygon/degree-bound content. [USABLE-BY-US — kills the graded-equivariant corner of the plane search space; consistent with and complementary to the GGV (rho,sigma) frame]
./RECON.md-73-- **Jelonek 2607.20597** (07-22): generic elements of suitable components of Jacobian-1 maps are counterexamples for n ≥ 3, d ≥ 6 — post-refutation "failure is generic" structure theorem. [CONTEXT]
./RECON.md:74:- **Meng–Yang 2607.22198v2** (07-24/27): Schur descent on the Alpöge map gives a 5-variable deg-14 Hessian-conjecture counterexample; ledger now "everything settled except HC(4) and JC(2)". [CONTEXT — sharpens that JC2 is the last survivor]
./RECON.md-75-- **Huq-Kuruvilla 2607.20968** (07-23): explicit char-2 counterexample to separable JC in dim 3 (answers Silberman's question on Speyer's blog). [CONTEXT]
./RECON.md-76-- **Mathieu/Gaussian-moments cluster:** Long 2607.18186 (07-20): explicit low-degree counterexamples to the Gaussian Moments Conjecture in dims 3,4 (routes derived from the JC counterexample); Long 2607.19012 (07-21): counterexamples to the xz-Conjecture and **the Mathieu Conjecture for SU(2)** — the Mathieu⇒JC proof route is now dead. **Wilson 2607.23887 (07-26): PROOF of the two-variable Gaussian Moments Conjecture by "face isolation" — Newton-polygon face analysis in two variables.** [USABLE-BY-US — same toolkit as ours (polygon faces/edges); the dim-2 positive result pattern continues; read for transferable face-isolation lemmas]
./RECON.md-77-- Migus 2607.21572v2 (07-23): generic degrees of real Keller maps with non-dense image; dim-2 statements conditional on planar JC. [CONTEXT]
./RECON.md-78-- No arXiv preprint yet from Alpöge himself (latest arXiv au:Alpoge item is Jan 2025); the counterexample's canonical writeups remain X + Tao/Speyer blogs + jacobianfun.org. [CONTEXT]
