   152	## 3. Literature analogue: Domrina-Orevkov's multi-dicritical split
   153	
   154	Read: refs/do.pdf (intro + §2); SHEET6.md §history; Domrina II metadata
   155	(mathnet im273). DO's stratification variable is the number of DICRITICAL
   156	COMPONENTS of the resolution at infinity (components of L~ on which F is
   157	non-constant with image not in L) — a finer/different count than Sigray's
   158	T_{a,pole} vertices (Sigray's poles carry Λ >= β >= 3 each; DO dicriticals
   159	carry >= 1 sheet each; at td=4 DO already faces multi-dicritical cases
   160	while Sigray's frame allows two poles first at td=6). The ANALOGY is
   161	structural, not an identification: in both frames the flagship kill is
   162	proved under a uniqueness hypothesis (DO paper I, p. 1: "we prove a
   163	particular case ... namely when f has ONE dicritical component. The
   164	complete proof will appear in the next paper"; Sigray: Prop 8.4's
   165	T_{a,pole} = {G}).
   166	
   167	How DO actually handled the split at td = 4: NOT by transferring the
   168	one-dicritical argument. Domrina's paper II ("Four-sheeted polynomial
   169	mappings of C². II. The general case", Izv. Math. 64 (2000)) redoes the
   170	whole case analysis over splice-diagram combinatorics (~19 configurations
   171	-> 8 final diagrams, killed by unimodularity/negative-definiteness/
   172	canonical-class arithmetic; SHEET6.md). Two lessons transfer:
   173	1. The multi-dicritical case is a GENUINE separate enumeration, roughly
   174	   the same size as the single case — matching what §§4-5 find here (a
   175	   new merge-step calculus, not a corollary of Prop 8.4).
   176	2. Their method has a PROVABLE ceiling (Orevkov's exotic-covering
   177	   examples, minimal degree 9; Egorov's 5-sheet example killed the
   178	   quasi-topological method at td=5 entirely) — so at td >= 5 the
   179	   analytic layer (Abhyankar/Puiseux arithmetic = Sigray's engine, or the
   180	   2008 proofs) is forced. There is NO ready-made multi-dicritical
   181	   argument at td=5 to imitate: td <= 5 never needs one in Sigray's frame
   182	   (3+3 > 5), and DO's td=4 multi-dicritical treatment is splice-diagram
   183	   arithmetic with no Eggers-Wall translation on record. What would be
   184	   td-specific input: the merge-vertex pattern lemma of §4a (two searrow
   185	   orbits in one root polynomial) — no analogue exists in DO because
   186	   their gluing is along divisor chains, not root polynomials.
