    28	## 0. Verdict in one paragraph
    29	
    30	The M=1 pre-merge chain step conserves a single rational invariant. Write
    31	each chain frame in the i-normalized coordinates ρ := D_F/deg(p_F) (full
    32	pattern degree) and set **w_F := (κ̄_F − ρ_F)/ν_F** with κ̄ := κ_F(1−π(F)).
    33	Then (i) every M=1 segment vertex is a *Puiseux characteristic vertex* of
    34	its own pole's series, with ν ≥ 2, and every chain edge is Prop 9.3 case
    35	(II) (§2); (ii) the chain step multiplies w by n/Δ, Δ := (n−1)ν_child + 1,
    36	where (ν_child, n) is the child's single-orbit pattern — so the infinite
    37	"l = 0" direction (n = 1) that makes depth unbounded **fixes w**, while
    38	every resonant step (n ≥ 2) requires Δ | num(w) and contracts w by a factor
    39	≤ 2/3 (§3–4); (iii) the entire jump-cell layer factors through w: for every
    40	μ = 1 edge into a merge, **κ̄_merge − D_merge/i = w** (the handshake), the
    41	merged-child data is (κ̄, D/i, ρ) = w·(dq, dp, 1)/(dq−dp), the join forces
    42	all arriving chains to share w, and per w the admissible cells are finite
    43	with ν_cell *determined* by (κ̄_merge, l) (§5). Hence the set of w-values
    44	over all depths is the finite computable closure W(w₀), realized by depth
    45	d₀ = gen(W)+2, and the map (segment depth) → (reachable jump-cell menu) is
    46	**constant beyond d₀**: DEPTH-INVARIANCE (Lemma, §6). At td = 6, m = 2:
    47	W = {2}, d₀ = 2, and the menu is *exactly* the promoted residue cell
    48	IIa (r,ν,l) = (2,3,1), M = 2, child (κ̄, D/i) = (5,3) — i.e. Q =
    49	(6,12,3,2,5) — reproducing the 351/351 empirical depth-invariance and
    50	reproving the root-meet kill in one line (root merges need w < 1). The
    51	jump-vertex book is therefore **finite per (m, td)** (§8).
