    55	## 1. Setting and normalization
    56	
    57	Notation as in SHEET6-MULTIPOLE.md §1. Fix a pole P_i ∈ T_{a,pole} with
    58	entry datum (a_i, b_i, ν_i) of type (α,β) (MP4: Q(P_i) = (a_iα, b_iα, ν_i,
    59	b_i, a_i(α+β)), St 5.2 + Not 8.1 + St 9.1 pp. 26/39/48). An **M=1 segment**
    60	is a maximal run F_0 → F_1 → … → F_d of the characteristic sequence
    61	(Prop 9.2, p. 50) with M ≡ 1, starting at the pole vertex (b_i = 1, forced
    62	at β-minimal and prime Λ_i by MP4) or at an M=1-emitting merge child, and
    63	ending at the last vertex before a merge vertex G (r(G) ≥ 2) or before
    64	(0,y). By MP5, every F_j with j ≥ 1 has reduced pattern a single simple
    65	ν-orbit: (dp, dq) = (ν_j, n_jν_j + 1), n_j ≥ 1, M = 1, λ = 0.
    66	
    67	Frames are taken **i-normalized** ("shape space" of the engines, P-free):
    68	
    69	- Q-datum (Not 9.1, p. 48): Q(F) = (D_F, deg(p_F), ν_F, M_F, κ̄_F),
    70	  κ̄_F := κ_F(1−π(F)).
    71	- ρ_F := D_F/deg(p_F) with deg(p_F) the FULL f-pattern degree (Not 3.10/
    72	  3.13, pp. 13/16); by Prop 8.1(i) (p. 40) p_full = ⊖(ξ^δ p_red)^i, so
    73	  deg(p_F) = i_F·deg(p_red) and ρ_F = (D_F/i_F)/deg(p_red).
    74	- **w_F := (κ̄_F − ρ_F)/ν_F.**
    75	
    76	ρ < κ̄ at every segment vertex (St 8.2, p. 41: deg q > deg p at μ = 1
    77	arrivals, and dp/dq = i-normalized slope ratio, Prop 9.3(b)), so w > 0.
    78	
    79	Equal-quotient transport (used throughout): for any edge F = G + c
    80	(F above G; Prop 3.2/St 3.17(i), pp. 17–18), deg(p_F) = mult(p_G, c) =
    81	i_G·mult(p_G^red, c) = i_G·μ_e, and μ_e | M_F = 1 by St 8.4 (p. 42) on M=1
    82	ancestry, so **deg(p_parent) = i_child** on every segment edge and every
    83	all-μ=1 merge edge. This is MP6(b) read at chain edges; it is what makes
    84	the (b)-equation of Prop 9.3 close in the ρ-coordinate.
