   142	## 3. DS2 (the orbit map and its conserved quantity)
   143	
   144	**Claim.** Let G → F be a segment edge (G = parent, F = G° single simple
   145	(ν_F, n_Fν_F+1)-orbit, μ = 1). Then, with Δ_F := (n_F−1)ν_F + 1 = dq−dp:
   146	
   147	    t     := (κ̄_G − ρ_G)/Δ_F        [edge scale]
   148	    n_e   =  t·ν_F − ρ_G  ∈ ℕ*       [Prop 9.3(a)-(b) edge parameter]
   149	    κ̄_F  =  (κ̄_G + n_e)/ν_G = t·dq_F/ν_G = w_G·dq_F/Δ_F
   150	    ρ_F   =  t/ν_G,      κ̄_F = ρ_F·dq_F
   151	    w_F   =  w_G · n_F/Δ_F.
   152	
   153	In particular: **n_F = 1 ("l = 0" step, the unbounded direction) fixes
   154	w_F = w_G for every admissible ν_F; n_F ≥ 2 ("resonant" step) contracts
   155	w_F ≤ (2/3)·w_G** (since ν_F ≥ 2 gives Δ_F ≥ 2n_F − 1).
   156	
   157	*Proof.* Case (II) applies (DS1(d)). Prop 9.3(b) (p. 50), i-normalized by
   158	deg(p_G) = i_F (§1, μ_e = 1): dp_F/dq_F = (ρ_G + n_e)/(κ̄_G + n_e). Both
   159	sides in lowest terms (gcd(ν_F, n_Fν_F+1) = 1), so ρ_G + n_e = tν_F and
   160	κ̄_G + n_e = t·dq_F with t = (κ̄_G − ρ_G)/(dq_F − dp_F) = w_Gν_G/Δ_F.
   161	Prop 9.3(d): κ̄_F = (κ̄_G + n_e)/ν_G = t·dq_F/ν_G. Prop 9.3(c) with
   162	deg(p_F) = deg(p_G)·ν_F = i_Fν_F: ρ_F = (ρ_G + n_e)/(ν_Gν_F) = t/ν_G.
   163	Then w_F = (κ̄_F − ρ_F)/ν_F = t(dq_F − 1)/(ν_Gν_F) = t·n_F/ν_G =
   164	w_G·n_F/Δ_F. Contraction: n_F/Δ_F = n_F/((n_F−1)ν_F+1) ≤ n_F/(2n_F−1)
   165	≤ 2/3 for n_F, ν_F ≥ 2. ∎
   166	
   167	**Remarks.** (R3) Robustness: a hypothetical ν_F = 1 step has Δ = n_F, so
   168	w_F = w_G for ALL n_F — the conservation does not even need DS1's
   169	exclusion of such steps (they conserve w trivially; DS1 is what grounds
   170	the case-(II) equations). (R4) The identity κ̄_F = ρ_F·dq_F means every
   171	post-entry frame satisfies κ̄ = ρ·(own dq); equivalently ρ = w/n and
   172	κ̄ = w(nν+1)/n: the frame is coded by (w, ν, n). (R5) The printed record
   173	itself displays the conservation: St 9.6(v) (p. 51), the thesis's own
   174	λ = 0 suffix family Q = ((6s+3)j, (4s+2)j, 2s+1, 2, 3s+3), has w ≡ 3/2
   175	for every s (machine check 5).
