   178	
   179	## 4. DS3 (the resonance budget: finitely many w-values)
   180	
   181	**Claim.** Write w_G = a/b in lowest terms. A resonant step (n_F ≥ 2)
   182	requires **Δ_F | a**; consequently ν_F ≤ a − 1, n_F ≤ (a+1)/2, there are
   183	at most as many resonant options as factorizations Δ − 1 = (n−1)ν with
   184	Δ | a, and num(w_F) ≤ (2/3)·a. Hence along ANY segment, of ANY depth, the
   185	number of resonant steps is < log_{3/2} num(w_0) + 1, and the set of
   186	w-values reachable from w_0 (over all depths) lies in the finite,
   187	explicitly computable closure
   188	
   189	    W(w_0) := closure of {w_0} under w ↦ w·n/Δ,  Δ | num(w), Δ ≥ 3,
   190	              Δ = (n−1)ν + 1, n ≥ 2, ν ≥ 2.
   191	
   192	*Proof.* κ̄_F ∈ ℤ (DS1(c)) and κ̄_F = t·dq_F/ν_G = w_G·dq_F/Δ_F =
   193	a·dq_F/(bΔ_F). Now gcd(Δ_F, dq_F) = gcd(Δ_F, dq_F − Δ_F) = gcd(Δ_F, ν_F)
   194	= gcd((n_F−1)ν_F + 1, ν_F) = 1, so bΔ_F | a·dq_F forces Δ_F | a. Then
   195	Δ_F ≥ ν_F + 1 and Δ_F ≥ 2n_F − 1 give the ranges, and num(w_F) divides
   196	a·n_F/Δ_F ≤ (2/3)a. A strictly decreasing chain of positive integers
   197	contracting by ≥ 1/3 per step has length < log_{3/2}(a_0) + 1. W(w_0) is
   198	finite because each generation divides-and-contracts the numerator. ∎
   199	
   200	**Entry values.** w_0 = (a_i(α+β) − a_i/b_i)/ν_i = a_i(b_i(α+β)−1)/(b_iν_i)
   201	(MP4 entry pin); on the M=1 axis b_i = 1: w_0 = a_i(α+β−1)/ν_i. Λ_i =
   202	a_ib_iαβ/ν_i ≤ td and mβ ≤ td bound a_i, α, β, ν_i, so num(w_0) ≤ td²/2
   203	crudely; everything downstream is computable per (m, td). At td = 6:
   204	w_0 = 1·(2+3−1)/2 = 2, and W(2) = {2} — no divisor Δ ≥ 3 of 2 exists, so
   205	**no resonant step is admissible at all** (machine check 2).
