2     A reformulation of the Jacobian conjecture
For given integers n ≥ 2, d ≥ 1 we denote by JEn,d an affine scheme of finite
type over Z representing the following functor. For any commutative ring
R the set JEn,d (R) is the set of endomorphisms f of R-algebra R[x1 , . . . , xn ]
such that

    • det (∂f (xi )/∂xj )1≤i,j≤n = 1 ∈ R[x1 , . . . , xn ],

    • deg(f (xi )) ≤ d     ∀i, 1 ≤ i ≤ n .

   We say that f as above is an endomorphism of degree ≤ d (and with
Jacobian 1). The ring of functions O(JEn,d ) is finitely generated, its gener-
ators are coefficients ci,α which appear in the universal endomorphism over
O(JEn,d ):                                 X
