xmodel/grok-approaches.md-150-**(a)** \(J(F)\in\mathbb C^*\) implies \(F\) is locally invertible; the formal inverse series exists. JC2 ⇔ that series is polynomial ⇔ all sufficiently high multi-degree coefficients vanish. Attack via Bass–Connell–Wright / Abhyankar / McKay–Wang inversion formulae, degree bounds on the inverse, or recursive vanishing of homogeneous components.
