Main ruling:

- The canonical inverse-Jacobian connection of a plane Keller map has identically zero $p$-curvature. This is automatic from $J(P,Q)=1$, not a new residue-A constraint.
- The banked depth-23/25 data lacks global $P,Q$, but no numerical run is needed: every genuine Keller completion would pass. The Artin–Schreier map $(x-x^p,y)$ shows the condition also passes nonautomorphisms.
- The Tsuchimoto/BKK dictionary runs from Weyl endomorphisms to symplectic center maps—not backward from commutative modular jets. A full plane Keller map yields a special $A_2$ endomorphism and its exact cotangent lift, but residue-A nonemptiness does not yet reach that object.
- Classification: **known-hollow as an independent residue-A attack; real and useful as a dictionary/scope lane.**

